    "suggested_action": "replace_ja_expression",
    "reason": "While '沙汰' (sata) can mean 'news' or 'information' in specific contexts (e.g., '音沙汰' for 'tidings/news', 'ご無沙汰' for 'long time no news'), it is not the general, natural, or most common Japanese word for 'news' that a learner would expect. Its other common meanings, such as 'affair,' 'judgment,' or 'rumor/scandal' (e.g., '不祥事沙汰'), make its 'news' sense narrower and less encompassing than the broad English 'news.' The loanword 'ニュース' is the standard and most natural equivalent for general 'news' (e.g., TV news, newspaper news).",
